Bash Notes
Command Substitution
-----------------------

Functions can modify the global scope.
If you use command substitution (var=$(func)) then it cannot modify that global scope.
Use "local" keyword in functions to avoid global scope changes.

New syntax (Bash 5.3+) allows for us to run the function outside of its own sub-shell but still capture the output.
Example: var=${ func; }
The space after the opening curly brace and the semicolon are required.
Slightly faster than using parenthesis because you have to create the sub-shell.
